{"title": "Tadpoling Centre", "pageid": 40009, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Tadpoling_Centre", "categories": ["Locations", "Act Two Locations"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Tadpoling_Centre.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fb/Tadpoling_Centre.png/300px-Tadpoling_Centre.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/fb/Tadpoling_Centre.png/450px-Tadpoling_Centre.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/fb/Tadpoling_Centre.png/600px-Tadpoling_Centre.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/fb/Tadpoling_Centre.png/300px-Tadpoling_Centre.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"223\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/fb/Tadpoling_Centre.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption><div class=\"noexcerpt navigation-not-searchable\">  Tadpoling Centre, with Neural Apparatus, full and empty pods seen  </div></figcaption></figure>The <b>Tadpoling Centre</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/Location\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Location\">Location</a> within <a href=\"/wiki/Shadow-Cursed_Lands\" title=\"Shadow-Cursed Lands\">Shadow-Cursed Lands</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Two\" title=\"Act Two\">Act Two</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/Baldur%27s_Gate_3\" title=\"Baldur's Gate 3\">Baldur's Gate 3</a>. It is where captives of the <a href=\"/wiki/Cult_of_the_Absolute\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Cult of the Absolute\">Cult of the Absolute</a> deemed worthy of further 'usage' are kept, tadpoled and sometimes turned into mind flayers. It can be reached (as the rest of the colony) only within <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Two\" title=\"Act Two\">Act Two</a> of the game and only after the initial fight with <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ketheric_Thorm\" title=\"Ketheric Thorm\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f2/Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png/25px-Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/f/f2/Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png/38px-Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/f/f2/Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png/50px-Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Ketheric Thorm\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/f/f2/Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png/25px-Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/f/f2/Portrait_Ketheric_Thorm.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Ketheric_Thorm\" title=\"Ketheric Thorm\">Ketheric Thorm</a>. \n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tadpoling_Centre\">Tadpoling Centre</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"How_to_find\">How to find</span></h3>\n<p>After descending into the colony and destroying fleshy membrane at the entrance, the party should go along the corridor. The Tadpoling Centre will be the first turn to the left, fenced off by a Flesh-Wrought Door.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"What.27s_inside\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"What's_inside\">What's inside</span></h3>\n<p>The Tadpoling Centre is a round room with four detached fleshy pillars and ten <a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Pod\" title=\"Mind Flayer Pod\">Mind Flayer Pods</a> along the walls (five to each side). Some are empty, some contain newly created mind flayers, but some keep characters who the party has already met in the game (see below). The room is 'maintained' by several <a href=\"/wiki/Intellect_Devourer\" title=\"Intellect Devourer\">Intellect Devourers</a> that run along back and forth the room and corridors.\n</p><p>Under each pod there is an active 'button', glowing either red (empty pod) or cyan (occupied pod). Interacting with cyan buttons will bring forth a Narrator line that briefly describe the person that is (or was) inside.\n</p><p>To the right of the entrance: \n</p>\n<ul><li>Empty pod</li>\n<li>Mind flayer</li>\n<li>Empty pod</li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Zevlor\" title=\"Zevlor\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/25px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/38px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/50px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Zevlor\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/25px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Zevlor\" title=\"Zevlor\">Zevlor</a></li>\n<li>Mind flayer</li></ul>\n<p>To the left of the entrance:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Empty pod (it, however, still preserves some scraps of <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ulder_Ravengard\" title=\"Ulder Ravengard\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d9/Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png/25px-Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/d/d9/Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png/38px-Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/d/d9/Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png/50px-Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Duke Ravengard's\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/d/d9/Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png/25px-Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/d/d9/Portrait_Ulder_Ravengard.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Ulder_Ravengard\" title=\"Ulder Ravengard\">Duke Ravengard's</a> personality)</li>\n<li>Mind flayer</li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Shuurga\" title=\"Shuurga\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/25px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/38px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/50px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Manip Shuurga\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/25px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Shuurga\" title=\"Shuurga\">Manip Shuurga</a></li>\n<li>Mind flayer</li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Yeva\" title=\"Yeva\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/25px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/38px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/50px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Gauntlet Yeva\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/25px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Yeva\" title=\"Yeva\">Gauntlet Yeva</a></li></ul>\n<p>Across the entrance is the corridor (leading to the room with larvae brine pools). To the right side of it stands a <a href=\"/wiki/Neural_Apparatus\" title=\"Neural Apparatus\">Neural Apparatus</a> that controls all of the pods in the room. Interacting with it enacts a dialogue where the party must decide the fate of all those who are still alive within the pods: either releasing them, killing them by purging the pods, or leaving them as they were. The latter allows to start the dialogue anew later.\n</p><p>Either option results in gaining <a href=\"/wiki/Approval\" title=\"Approval\">Approval/Disapproval</a> from different party members (f.e., releasing the captives is approved by <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Shadowheart\" title=\"Shadowheart\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/25px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/38px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/50px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Shadowheart\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png/25px-Portrait_Shadowheart.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/7e/Portrait_Shadowheart.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Shadowheart\" title=\"Shadowheart\">Shadowheart</a> and <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Karlach\" title=\"Karlach\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b2/Portrait_Karlach.png/25px-Portrait_Karlach.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/b2/Portrait_Karlach.png/38px-Portrait_Karlach.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/b2/Portrait_Karlach.png/50px-Portrait_Karlach.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Karlach\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/b2/Portrait_Karlach.png/25px-Portrait_Karlach.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/b2/Portrait_Karlach.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Karlach\" title=\"Karlach\">Karlach</a> and disapproved by <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Astarion\" title=\"Astarion\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1b/Portrait_Astarion.png/25px-Portrait_Astarion.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/1b/Portrait_Astarion.png/38px-Portrait_Astarion.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/1b/Portrait_Astarion.png/50px-Portrait_Astarion.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Astarion\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1b/Portrait_Astarion.png/25px-Portrait_Astarion.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/1b/Portrait_Astarion.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Astarion\" title=\"Astarion\">Astarion</a>, <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Minthara\" title=\"Minthara\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8e/Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png/25px-Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/8e/Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png/38px-Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/8e/Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png/50px-Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Minthara\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8e/Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png/25px-Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/8e/Portrait_Minthara_%28263%29.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Minthara\" title=\"Minthara\">Minthara</a>, and <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lae%27zel\" title=\"Lae'zel\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/86/Portrait_Lae%27zel.png/25px-Portrait_Lae%27zel.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/86/Portrait_Lae%27zel.png/38px-Portrait_Lae%27zel.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/86/Portrait_Lae%27zel.png/50px-Portrait_Lae%27zel.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Lae'zel\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/86/Portrait_Lae%27zel.png/25px-Portrait_Lae%27zel.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/86/Portrait_Lae%27zel.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Lae%27zel\" title=\"Lae'zel\">Lae'zel</a>).\n</p><p>The pods cannot be operated separately, so all pod inhabitants who are still alive must be either killed or freed at once. A battle starts if the inhabitants are freed, as all four released mind flayers instantaneously turn hostile and attack. However, the other characters who stayed within the pods intact and were freed become allies and fight along the party. The <a href=\"/wiki/Intellect_Devourer\" title=\"Intellect Devourer\">Intellect Devourers</a> running around join the battle too, siding with the mind flayers.\n</p><p>Zevlor and the other survivors can potentially turn hostile if they take damage from the party, even unintentionally.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"After_the_battle\">After the battle</span></h3>\n<p>After resolving the battle the party can speak with the allies who survived.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Gauntlet Yeva tells that Duke Ravengard was taken from his pod not very long before, still human and able to resist the convoy guards.</li>\n<li>Manip Shuurga tells just lament herself being unable to help the Duke.</li>\n<li>Talking to Zevlor reveals what actually happened to him when the refugees' caravan had been attacked by cultists upon entering the <a href=\"/wiki/Shadow-Cursed_Lands\" title=\"Shadow-Cursed Lands\">Shadow-Cursed Lands</a>. This dialogue ends the quest <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Find_Zevlor\" title=\"Find Zevlor\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/33px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/44px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Find Zevlor\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Find_Zevlor\" title=\"Find Zevlor\">Find Zevlor</a>. After that, Zevlor says he is going to gather whoever he can around the colony and guide them out to safety. If the party convince the former Hellrider that he still might be worthy, Zevlor will be available in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Three\" title=\"Act Three\">Act Three</a> as an aidee in the final battle through the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Gather_Your_Allies\" title=\"Gather Your Allies\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/33px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/44px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Gather Your Allies\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Gather_Your_Allies\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Gather Your Allies\">Gather Your Allies</a> quest.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Brine_pools_room\">Brine pools room</span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/90/Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg/300px-Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/90/Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg/450px-Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/90/Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg/600px-Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/90/Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg/300px-Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/90/Stimona-milanova-stimona-milanova-mfc-4.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>A view of the brine pools</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Behind the Tadpoling Centre is another room with a cascade of several brine pools alike the one that the party had already seen on the nautiloid. These are empty of larvae, and this fact discomposes and bemuses the <a href=\"/wiki/Dream_Guardian\" title=\"Dream Guardian\">Dream Guardian</a>. Interacting with the leftmost brine pool gives a chance to catch one last <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-story\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen\" title=\"Mind Flayer Parasite Specimen\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/20px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/30px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/40px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png/20px-Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/91/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen_Item_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Parasite_Specimen\" title=\"Mind Flayer Parasite Specimen\">Mind Flayer Parasite Specimen</a> (requires a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;16 Perception Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;16 <a href=\"/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\">Perception</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a>).\n</p><p>In this room two more detached Mind Flayer Pods can be found, one of which contains the captured <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mizora\" title=\"Mizora\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/25px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/38px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/50px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Mizora\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/25px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mizora\" title=\"Mizora\">Mizora</a>. This is the point when the party can start helping <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Wyll\" title=\"Wyll\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6d/Portrait_Wyll.png/25px-Portrait_Wyll.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6d/Portrait_Wyll.png/38px-Portrait_Wyll.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/6d/Portrait_Wyll.png/50px-Portrait_Wyll.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Wyll\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6d/Portrait_Wyll.png/25px-Portrait_Wyll.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/6d/Portrait_Wyll.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Wyll\" title=\"Wyll\">Wyll</a>, if he was recruited and is still alive to break his <a href=\"/wiki/Warlock\" title=\"Warlock\">Warlock</a> pact — in order to do this, passing a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;16 Intimidation Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;16 <a href=\"/wiki/Intimidation\" title=\"Intimidation\">Intimidation</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a> while speaking with Mizora is necessary.\n</p><p>Her pod has its own controlling panel with two switches marked by illithid symbols that must first be deciphered by a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;10 Arcana Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;10 <a href=\"/wiki/Arcana\" title=\"Arcana\">Arcana</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a>. One frees the cambion, while another annihilates her. <b>Killing Mizora in the pod instantly kills Wyll, too (even if he is already dead)</b>. It is also possible to smash the pod open, requiring a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;14 Strength Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;14 <a href=\"/wiki/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">Strength</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a>.\n</p><p>If saved, and convinced to reward the party through a successful <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;14 Persuasion Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;14 <a href=\"/wiki/Persuasion\" title=\"Persuasion\">Persuasion</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a>, Mizora rewards Wyll with the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-very-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Infernal_Rapier\" title=\"Infernal Rapier\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Infernal_Rapier\" title=\"Infernal Rapier\">Infernal Rapier</a> (only possible if Wyll is in the party during the rescue). Mischievous as ever, she also lifts Wyll's restriction on talking about their pact before leaving.\n</p><p>The Ruptured Mind Flayer Pod to the left of Mizora is of particular note to <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Dark_Urge\" title=\"The Dark Urge\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8c/Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png/25px-Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/8c/Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png/38px-Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/8c/Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png/50px-Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"The Dark Urge\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/8c/Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png/25px-Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/8c/Portrait_The_Dark_Urge.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/The_Dark_Urge\" title=\"The Dark Urge\">The Dark Urge</a>. A <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;10 Investigation Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;10 <a href=\"/wiki/Investigation\" title=\"Investigation\">Investigation</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a> reveals that the blood found on the casing is still fresh, and Astarion, if present, can confirm that the blood undoubtedly belongs to The Dark Urge. With a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;10 Charisma Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;10 <a href=\"/wiki/Charisma\" title=\"Charisma\">Charisma</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a>, memories of their imprisonment come flooding back and in them the taunts and laughter of the <a href=\"/wiki/Orin\" title=\"Orin\">woman</a> who betrayed them, adding an extra note in their <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Open_Your_Scars\" title=\"Open Your Scars\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/33px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/44px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Open Your Scars\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png/22px-Quest_Map_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/69/Quest_Map_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Open_Your_Scars\" title=\"Open Your Scars\">Open Your Scars</a> quest.\n</p><p>In this room, there is also a book that partially reveals the peculiarities of the tadpoled condition.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Characters\">Characters</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mizora\" title=\"Mizora\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/30px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/45px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/60px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Mizora\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png/30px-Portrait_Mizora.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/7/77/Portrait_Mizora.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mizora\" title=\"Mizora\">Mizora</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Shuurga\" title=\"Shuurga\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/30px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/45px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/60px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Manip Shuurga\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png/30px-Portrait_Shuurga.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/5/59/Portrait_Shuurga.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Shuurga\" title=\"Shuurga\">Manip Shuurga</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Yeva\" title=\"Yeva\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/30px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/45px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/60px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Gauntlet Yeva\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png/30px-Portrait_Yeva.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/6a/Portrait_Yeva.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Yeva\" title=\"Yeva\">Gauntlet Yeva</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Zevlor\" title=\"Zevlor\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/30px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/45px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/60px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Zevlor\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png/30px-Portrait_Zevlor.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/e7/Portrait_Zevlor.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Zevlor\" title=\"Zevlor\">Zevlor</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Loot\">Loot</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-block\" style=\"gap: 6px\"><span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-very-rare\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Infernal_Rapier\" title=\"Infernal Rapier\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/45px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/60px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"30\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/5/5a/Infernal_Rapier_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Infernal_Rapier\" title=\"Infernal Rapier\">Infernal Rapier</a></span> - reward for freeing Mizora</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h2>\n<div class=\"notebegin\">\n<ul><li>In <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Three\" title=\"Act Three\">Act Three</a>, when the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Emperor\" title=\"The Emperor\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/25px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/38px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/50px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Emperor\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png/25px-Portrait_The_Emperor.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/c/c6/Portrait_The_Emperor.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/The_Emperor\" title=\"The Emperor\">Emperor</a> recalls discovering the colony under <a href=\"/wiki/Moonrise_Towers\" title=\"Moonrise Towers\">Moonrise Towers</a> and being captured, his memories do not contain pictures of Tadpoling Centre. It remembers his human form simply tied to a chair when being infected with a tadpole.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"navbox-styles\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r138587\">.mw-parser-output .hlist dl,.mw-parser-output .hlist ul,.mw-parser-output .bg3wiki-horizontlist dl,.mw-parser-output .bg3